{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()"},"metadata":{"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L36","fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["Trees"]}],"extendedModule":"Trees"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly. A mirrored tree draws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the reflection of the drawing, and isomorphic subtrees are drawn identically up to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"translation. Separations and centring give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":". The even spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps, so values such as ±5\/6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"occur and are rounded, and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Experience 20(7), 1990.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees":{"title":"Trees","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Drawing","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","abstract":[{"text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drawing","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree":{"kind":"symbol","title":"RootedTree","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/